WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.074
Support us and become VIP member 
to remove all ads from www.OpenSubtitles.org

2
00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:31.800
Blake.

3
00:01:33.303 --> 00:01:34.303
Blake.

4
00:01:35.555 --> 00:01:36.555
Sorry. sarge.

5
00:01:37.182 --> 00:01:40.720
Pick a man. bring your kit.

6
00:01:40.810 --> 00:01:41.810
Yes. sarge.

7
00:02:04.376 --> 00:02:05.376
Don't dawdle.

8
00:02:05.877 --> 00:02:06.877
No. sarge.

9
00:02:16.346 --> 00:02:17.631
Did they feed us?

10
00:02:18.473 --> 00:02:20.009
No. Just mail.

11
00:02:41.329 --> 00:02:42.739
Myrtle's having puppies.

12
00:02:45.750 --> 00:02:46.910
You get anything?

13
00:02:47.502 --> 00:02:48.617
No.

14
00:02:50.296 --> 00:02:52.207
I'm bloody starvin'. aren't you?

15
00:02:53.341 --> 00:02:55.707
Thought we might get
some decent grub out here.

16
00:02:56.344 --> 00:02:59.086
It was the only reason
I decided against the priesthood.

17
00:03:04.978 --> 00:03:06.263
What you got there?

18
00:03:06.354 --> 00:03:07.354
Ham and bread.

19
00:03:08.064 --> 00:03:09.270
Where did you find that?

20
00:03:10.191 --> 00:03:11.476
I have my uses.

21
00:03:13.611 --> 00:03:14.611
Here.

22
00:03:20.243 --> 00:03:21.699
Tastes like old shoe.

23
00:03:22.495 --> 00:03:25.487
Cheer up. This time next week.
it'll be chicken dinner.

24
00:03:26.833 --> 00:03:27.833
Not me.

25
00:03:29.127 --> 00:03:30.367
My leave got canceled.

26
00:03:31.296 --> 00:03:32.296
They say why?

27
00:03:33.465 --> 00:03:34.465
No idea.

28
00:03:36.217 --> 00:03:37.923
It's easier not to go back at all.

29
00:03:41.556 --> 00:03:42.556
Coming through!

30
00:03:49.397 --> 00:03:51.809
Something's up. Did you hear anything?

31
00:03:52.358 --> 00:03:53.358
No.

32
00:03:54.527 --> 00:03:55.812
Has to be the push. right?

33
00:03:57.739 --> 00:03:59.730
Ten Bob says we're going up.

34
00:04:00.492 --> 00:04:01.777
I'm not taking that bet.

35
00:04:02.619 --> 00:04:04.450
Why? 'Cause you know I'm right?

36
00:04:04.537 --> 00:04:07.404
No. because you haven't got ten Bob.

37
00:04:11.336 --> 00:04:12.746
In your own time. gentlemen.

38
00:04:13.838 --> 00:04:16.295
- Is there any news. sarge?
- News of what?

39
00:04:16.382 --> 00:04:18.873
The big push.
It was supposed to happen weeks ago.

40
00:04:18.968 --> 00:04:20.583
They told us we'd be home by Christmas.

41
00:04:20.678 --> 00:04:22.964
Yes. well. sorry to disrupt
your crowded schedule. Blake.

42
00:04:23.056 --> 00:04:25.388
but the brass hats
didn't fancy it in the snow.

43
00:04:25.475 --> 00:04:27.841
More's the pity. sarge.
I could've done with some Turkey.

44
00:04:27.936 --> 00:04:30.894
Well. I'll make sure to relay
your displeasure to command.

45
00:04:30.980 --> 00:04:32.845
So. what's on the cards then.
sergeant?

46
00:04:32.941 --> 00:04:34.647
The hun are up to something.

47
00:04:34.734 --> 00:04:35.769
Any idea what?

48
00:04:35.860 --> 00:04:38.567
No. But it's about to ruin our weekend.

49
00:04:46.037 --> 00:04:47.368
Now. listen.

50
00:04:47.455 --> 00:04:49.787
Erinmore is inside. so tidy yourselves up.

51
00:04:51.292 --> 00:04:54.500
Never know. might be mentions
in dispatches for this one...

52
00:04:56.422 --> 00:04:57.787
If you don't bugger it up.

53
00:05:01.052 --> 00:05:03.259
Must be something big
if the general's here.

54
00:05:13.523 --> 00:05:15.764
Lance corporals
Blake and Schofield. sir.

55
00:05:18.611 --> 00:05:20.147
Which one of you is Blake?

56
00:05:20.238 --> 00:05:21.238
Sir.

57
00:05:21.906 --> 00:05:24.568
You have a brother.
a lieutenant in the 2nd devons?

58
00:05:25.159 --> 00:05:27.366
Yes. sir. Joseph Blake. Is he...

59
00:05:27.453 --> 00:05:29.239
Alive. As far as I know.

60
00:05:30.331 --> 00:05:32.788
And with your help.
I'd like to keep it that way.

61
00:05:33.626 --> 00:05:36.083
Sanders tells me
you're good with maps. That true?

62
00:05:36.838 --> 00:05:37.838
Good enough. sir.

63
00:05:39.132 --> 00:05:40.132
So...

64
00:05:42.135 --> 00:05:44.046
We are here.

65
00:05:45.054 --> 00:05:47.921
The 2nd devons are advancing here.

66
00:05:48.516 --> 00:05:50.381
How long will it take you to get there?

67
00:05:51.895 --> 00:05:53.385
I don't understand. sir.

68
00:05:53.479 --> 00:05:56.266
- Sir. that land is held by the Germans.
- Germans have gone.

69
00:05:57.650 --> 00:05:59.436
Don't get your hopes up.

70
00:05:59.527 --> 00:06:02.018
It appears to be a strategic withdrawal.

71
00:06:03.197 --> 00:06:07.065
They seem to have created a new line.
nine miles back here by the looks of it.

72
00:06:07.660 --> 00:06:09.946
Colonel MacKenzie
is in command of the 2nd.

73
00:06:10.914 --> 00:06:14.623
He sent word yesterday morning
he was going after the retreating Germans.

74
00:06:15.460 --> 00:06:17.917
He is convinced he has them on the run.

75
00:06:18.004 --> 00:06:20.962
that if he can break their lines now.
he will turn the tide.

76
00:06:22.425 --> 00:06:23.425
He is wrong.

77
00:06:24.135 --> 00:06:28.674
Colonel MacKenzie has not seen
these aerials of the enemy's new line.

78
00:06:28.765 --> 00:06:30.175
Come around here. gentlemen.

79
00:06:32.435 --> 00:06:35.518
Three miles deep.
field fortifications. defenses.

80
00:06:35.605 --> 00:06:38.187
artillery the like of which
we've never seen before.

81
00:06:39.567 --> 00:06:42.684
The 2nd are due to attack the line
shortly after dawn tomorrow.

82
00:06:43.363 --> 00:06:45.274
They have no idea
what they're in for.

83
00:06:46.115 --> 00:06:47.355
And we can't warn them.

84
00:06:51.412 --> 00:06:54.529
Your orders are to get to the 2nd
at croisilles wood.

85
00:06:54.624 --> 00:06:57.161
one mile southeast
of the town of ecoust.

86
00:06:58.086 --> 00:07:00.042
Deliver this to colonel MacKenzie.

87
00:07:00.129 --> 00:07:03.041
It is a direct order
to call off tomorrow morning's attack.

88
00:07:03.716 --> 00:07:05.798
If you don't.
it will be a massacre.

89
00:07:06.594 --> 00:07:10.462
We will lose two battalions.
1.600 men. your brother among them.

90
00:07:11.933 --> 00:07:13.924
Do you think
you can get there in time?

91
00:07:14.018 --> 00:07:15.098
Yes. sir.

92
00:07:15.186 --> 00:07:16.551
Any questions?

93
00:07:16.646 --> 00:07:18.102
- No. sir.
- Good.

94
00:07:18.523 --> 00:07:19.729
Over to you. lieutenant.

95
00:07:22.777 --> 00:07:24.142
Supplies. gentlemen.

96
00:07:25.613 --> 00:07:29.697
Map. torches. grenades.
and a couple of little treats.

97
00:07:30.910 --> 00:07:33.868
Leave immediately. Take this trench west
up on sauchiehall street.

98
00:07:33.955 --> 00:07:36.196
Then northwest on paradise alley
at the front.

99
00:07:36.290 --> 00:07:39.123
Continue along the front line
until you find the Yorks.

100
00:07:39.210 --> 00:07:40.746
Give this note to major Stevenson.

101
00:07:40.837 --> 00:07:43.499
He's holding the line
at the shortest span of no-man's-land.

102
00:07:43.589 --> 00:07:44.920
You'll cross there.

103
00:07:45.508 --> 00:07:47.419
It'll be daylight. sir.
They'll see us.

104
00:07:47.510 --> 00:07:49.250
There's no need to be concerned.

105
00:07:49.345 --> 00:07:51.006
You should meet no resistance.

106
00:07:57.103 --> 00:07:59.640
Sir. is... is it just us?

107
00:08:00.606 --> 00:08:05.066
"Down to gehenna or up to the throne.
he travels the fastest who travels alone."

108
00:08:06.029 --> 00:08:08.611
- Wouldn't you say. lieutenant?
- Yes. sir. I would.

109
00:08:11.159 --> 00:08:12.159
Good luck.

110
00:08:22.503 --> 00:08:24.710
Blake. let's talk about this
for a minute.

111
00:08:24.797 --> 00:08:25.797
Why?

112
00:08:33.473 --> 00:08:34.473
Blakel

113
00:08:41.856 --> 00:08:43.221
We just need to think about it.

114
00:08:43.316 --> 00:08:45.523
There's nothing to think about.
It's my big brother.

115
00:08:45.610 --> 00:08:49.023
- We should at least wait until it's dark.
- Erinmore said to leave immediately.

116
00:08:49.113 --> 00:08:51.149
Erinmore's
never seen ho-man's-land.

117
00:08:51.240 --> 00:08:52.821
We won't make it ten yards.

118
00:08:52.909 --> 00:08:53.819
If we just wait...

119
00:08:53.910 --> 00:08:56.492
You heard him.
He said the boche have gone.

120
00:08:57.038 --> 00:08:59.029
Is that why he gave us grenades?

121
00:09:10.176 --> 00:09:12.212
- Watch where you're going.
- Sorry.

122
00:09:21.437 --> 00:09:23.428
All I'm saying is that we wait.

123
00:09:23.898 --> 00:09:26.890
Yes. you would say that
'cause it's not your brother. is it?

124
00:09:29.695 --> 00:09:33.313
Look. the last time I was told
the Germans were gone. it didn't end well.

125
00:09:34.283 --> 00:09:36.319
You don't know. Blake.
You weren't there.

126
00:09:39.163 --> 00:09:40.949
Excuse me. Excuse me.

127
00:09:41.040 --> 00:09:43.031
Excuse me.

128
00:09:47.380 --> 00:09:49.462
You're going up the down trench.
you bloody idiot.

129
00:09:49.549 --> 00:09:50.914
Orders of the general. sir.

130
00:10:03.896 --> 00:10:05.978
All right.
say the boche have gone.

131
00:10:06.649 --> 00:10:08.731
Nine miles would take us.
what. six hours?

132
00:10:08.818 --> 00:10:10.308
Eight at the very most.

133
00:10:10.403 --> 00:10:12.439
So. we've got time to wait
until the sun sets.

134
00:10:12.530 --> 00:10:13.924
- It's enemy territory.
- Otherwise we'll be wide open.

135
00:10:13.948 --> 00:10:15.628
We've got no idea what we're walking into.

136
00:10:15.658 --> 00:10:19.776
Blake. if we're not clever about this.
no one will get to your brother.

137
00:10:20.872 --> 00:10:21.872
I will.

138
00:10:24.458 --> 00:10:26.665
We're here. This is the front line.

139
00:10:29.380 --> 00:10:30.870
Now we need to find the Yorks.

140
00:11:16.093 --> 00:11:17.629
Sorry. mate.

141
00:11:18.221 --> 00:11:20.324
- Watch who you're shoving.
- Get out of the way.

142
00:11:20.348 --> 00:11:22.576
Who the fuck do you think you are.
pushing wounded soldiers?

143
00:11:22.600 --> 00:11:23.965
I didn't know. Let go of me!

144
00:11:24.060 --> 00:11:26.551
Arsehole knocked down our sergeant.
The man's fucking wounded!

145
00:11:26.646 --> 00:11:28.728
All right. I'm sorry.
All right? I'm sorry!

146
00:11:28.814 --> 00:11:30.083
- We're on commission.
- Just let me through.

147
00:11:30.107 --> 00:11:32.143
- Orders from the general.
- Just let me through.

148
00:11:33.486 --> 00:11:34.486
Get out of the way.

149
00:11:36.280 --> 00:11:38.692
All right.
Just watch where you're going.

150
00:12:08.521 --> 00:12:09.521
It's bloody quiet.

151
00:12:10.940 --> 00:12:12.601
Was it like this before thiepval?

152
00:12:13.442 --> 00:12:14.442
Don't remember.

153
00:12:15.444 --> 00:12:16.900
You don't remember the somme?

154
00:12:17.405 --> 00:12:19.691
- Not really.
- Hey. mind us. Come on.

155
00:12:22.159 --> 00:12:23.865
Well. you did all right out of it.

156
00:12:24.829 --> 00:12:26.160
At least wear your ribbon.

157
00:12:27.248 --> 00:12:28.579
Don't have it anymore.

158
00:12:29.583 --> 00:12:32.074
What? You lost your medal?

159
00:12:32.169 --> 00:12:33.375
Heads down. boys.

160
00:12:34.880 --> 00:12:36.962
Come on. lads. Keep digging.

161
00:12:41.095 --> 00:12:42.095
Stay low.

162
00:12:49.312 --> 00:12:50.893
For god's sake. careful there.

163
00:12:50.980 --> 00:12:52.595
You're stepping on the dead.

164
00:12:52.690 --> 00:12:53.770
That's our sergeant.

165
00:12:54.442 --> 00:12:56.842
Be better washing them out of this dugout
with a bloody hose.

166
00:12:56.902 --> 00:12:58.517
Do you know where the Yorks are?

167
00:12:58.612 --> 00:13:01.069
The next bend.
you'll be standing on top of half of them.

168
00:13:01.157 --> 00:13:02.567
Shot to hell two nights ago.

169
00:13:12.293 --> 00:13:13.293
Yorks?

170
00:13:13.711 --> 00:13:14.791
Yes. corp.

171
00:13:14.879 --> 00:13:16.085
Where's major Stevenson?

172
00:13:16.630 --> 00:13:18.962
Was killed.
Couple of nights ago. corporal.

173
00:13:19.633 --> 00:13:21.169
Lieutenant Leslie has command.

174
00:13:21.719 --> 00:13:22.919
Where can we find him?

175
00:13:23.596 --> 00:13:24.631
Next dugout.

176
00:13:32.813 --> 00:13:33.813
Here.

177
00:13:39.028 --> 00:13:40.028
Sir?

178
00:13:40.696 --> 00:13:42.812
Lieutenant Leslie. sir?
What is it?

179
00:13:42.907 --> 00:13:44.772
We have a message
from general erinmore.

180
00:13:44.867 --> 00:13:46.573
- Are you our relief?
- No. sir.

181
00:13:46.660 --> 00:13:48.571
Then when the fucking hell are they due?

182
00:13:48.662 --> 00:13:51.199
We don't know. sir.
but we've got orders to cross here.

183
00:13:51.290 --> 00:13:53.076
That is the German front line.

184
00:13:53.167 --> 00:13:54.167
We know. sir.

185
00:13:54.627 --> 00:13:56.208
If you'll just take the letter.

186
00:13:58.464 --> 00:14:00.000
Settle a bet. What day is it?

187
00:14:01.217 --> 00:14:02.252
Friday.

188
00:14:02.343 --> 00:14:04.083
Friday? Well. none of us was right.

189
00:14:04.178 --> 00:14:06.885
- This idiot thought it was Tuesday.
- Sorry. sir.

190
00:14:08.682 --> 00:14:10.889
Are they out of their fucking minds?

191
00:14:10.976 --> 00:14:13.968
One slow night. the brass think
the hun have just gone home?

192
00:14:14.063 --> 00:14:15.678
Do you think they're wrong. sir?

193
00:14:16.857 --> 00:14:19.314
We lost an officer and three men
two nights ago.

194
00:14:19.402 --> 00:14:21.063
They were shot to bits patching up wire.

195
00:14:21.153 --> 00:14:23.986
We dragged two of them back here.
Needn't have bothered...

196
00:14:24.073 --> 00:14:27.190
Sir. the general is sure
the enemy have withdrawn.

197
00:14:27.284 --> 00:14:29.275
- There are aerials of the new line...
- Shut up.

198
00:14:29.370 --> 00:14:31.861
We fought and died
over every inch of this fucking place.

199
00:14:31.956 --> 00:14:34.322
Now they suddenly give us miles.
It's a trap.

200
00:14:38.212 --> 00:14:40.373
But chin up.
There's a medal in it. for sure.

201
00:14:40.464 --> 00:14:43.206
Nothing like a scrap of ribbon
to cheer up a widow.

202
00:14:45.970 --> 00:14:47.380
All right.

203
00:14:50.224 --> 00:14:51.885
Where's the nearest way through. sir?

204
00:14:51.976 --> 00:14:54.843
Our wire's a mess.
but there is a path through of sorts.

205
00:14:54.937 --> 00:14:56.893
Rushworth. let him look.

206
00:15:01.902 --> 00:15:04.018
Straight ahead to the left.
past the dead horses.

207
00:15:04.113 --> 00:15:05.819
There's a gap directly behind them.

208
00:15:06.824 --> 00:15:09.861
Useful because if it's dark.
you follow the stench.

209
00:15:09.952 --> 00:15:13.740
When you get to the second wire.
look out for the bowing chap.

210
00:15:13.831 --> 00:15:15.696
There's a small break just beside him.

211
00:15:15.791 --> 00:15:18.498
The German line
is 150-odd yards after that.

212
00:15:19.170 --> 00:15:21.957
Watch out for the craters.
They're deeper than they look.

213
00:15:22.047 --> 00:15:23.833
If you fall in. there's no getting out.

214
00:15:24.383 --> 00:15:25.383
This way.

215
00:15:27.428 --> 00:15:28.428
Wake up. kilgour.

216
00:15:29.013 --> 00:15:30.344
Bloody waste of space.

217
00:15:30.431 --> 00:15:32.342
Any cover. sir?
Anywhere to jump off from?

218
00:15:32.433 --> 00:15:34.594
No. The sap trench
was blown to hell weeks ago.

219
00:15:34.685 --> 00:15:36.095
It was full of bodies. anyway.

220
00:15:36.187 --> 00:15:38.098
Your best bet is to pop over here.

221
00:15:42.193 --> 00:15:44.479
If you do get shot.
try to make it back to the wire.

222
00:15:44.570 --> 00:15:46.561
We won't come after you.
not till it's dark.

223
00:15:46.655 --> 00:15:50.773
And if by some fucking miracle
you do make it. send up a flare.

224
00:15:50.868 --> 00:15:51.983
Don't have any. sir.

225
00:15:52.870 --> 00:15:55.236
Well. get him one. kilgour.
Make yourself useful.

226
00:15:55.331 --> 00:15:56.331
Yes. sir.

227
00:15:59.543 --> 00:16:02.785
Through this holy unction.
may the lord pardon you your faults

228
00:16:02.880 --> 00:16:04.711
and whatever sins
thou has committed.

229
00:16:08.093 --> 00:16:10.049
I do hate losing these to the hun.

230
00:16:10.137 --> 00:16:14.631
So. when they start shooting at you.
could you be so kind as to throw it back.

231
00:16:14.725 --> 00:16:15.805
There's a good chap.

232
00:16:19.146 --> 00:16:20.146
Cheerio.

233
00:16:28.030 --> 00:16:29.030
You sure?

234
00:16:30.533 --> 00:16:31.648
Yes.

235
00:16:37.957 --> 00:16:38.957
Age before beauty.

236
00:18:26.982 --> 00:18:27.982
You all right?

237
00:18:30.778 --> 00:18:31.778
Look for cover.

238
00:18:54.009 --> 00:18:55.009
Sap trench.

239
00:20:22.973 --> 00:20:23.973
Stay still.

240
00:20:32.983 --> 00:20:34.189
They're ours.

241
00:20:35.819 --> 00:20:37.730
Keep going. We're halfway.

242
00:21:42.719 --> 00:21:44.710
There's a gap. In the wire.

243
00:22:42.821 --> 00:22:44.027
Sco.

244
00:23:08.138 --> 00:23:09.799
There. That's the front line.

245
00:23:35.582 --> 00:23:36.788
Fuck me.

246
00:23:37.668 --> 00:23:39.033
They really have gone.

247
00:24:00.315 --> 00:24:01.521
Your hand all right?

248
00:24:03.193 --> 00:24:04.899
Put it through an effing German.

249
00:24:06.738 --> 00:24:07.773
Patch it up.

250
00:24:08.365 --> 00:24:10.196
You'll be wanking again in no time.

251
00:24:11.743 --> 00:24:12.743
Wrong hand.

252
00:24:43.525 --> 00:24:44.640
They're not long gone.

253
00:25:08.550 --> 00:25:09.550
No good.

254
00:25:32.074 --> 00:25:33.074
Blocked.

255
00:25:34.117 --> 00:25:35.527
This might be a way through.

256
00:25:51.426 --> 00:25:52.632
Jesus.

257
00:26:01.103 --> 00:26:02.343
Look at this.

258
00:26:03.855 --> 00:26:05.061
It's massive.

259
00:26:08.151 --> 00:26:09.732
They built all this.

260
00:26:56.491 --> 00:26:57.856
Here's our way through.

261
00:26:58.410 --> 00:26:59.410
Sco.

262
00:27:01.288 --> 00:27:02.288
How 'bout this?

263
00:27:07.085 --> 00:27:08.325
Bloody hell.

264
00:27:11.423 --> 00:27:13.414
Even their rats are bigger than ours.

265
00:27:20.640 --> 00:27:22.255
What do you think's in the bags?

266
00:27:23.435 --> 00:27:25.016
You cannot be that hungry.

267
00:27:31.526 --> 00:27:34.313
Look at him.
Cocky little bastard.

268
00:27:35.447 --> 00:27:37.187
You could eat this. though.

269
00:27:37.282 --> 00:27:38.522
What is it?

270
00:27:38.617 --> 00:27:39.777
Boche dog meat.

271
00:27:41.953 --> 00:27:43.284
What's in the other boxes?

272
00:27:45.665 --> 00:27:47.701
- What's wrong?
- Trip wire.

273
00:27:48.835 --> 00:27:49.915
Don't move.

274
00:27:50.962 --> 00:27:52.168
Where is it?

275
00:27:54.716 --> 00:27:56.331
Goes from here to the door.

276
00:27:59.221 --> 00:28:01.587
- Oh! Jesus!
- Oh. no!

277
00:28:11.107 --> 00:28:13.018
Sco!

278
00:28:19.658 --> 00:28:21.569
Sco?

279
00:28:24.955 --> 00:28:25.955
Sco!

280
00:28:29.292 --> 00:28:31.908
Sco! Sco.

281
00:28:37.926 --> 00:28:38.926
Sco!

282
00:28:43.390 --> 00:28:45.301
Sco. Sco?

283
00:28:46.017 --> 00:28:48.349
Wake up. Wake up!

284
00:28:51.231 --> 00:28:52.641
Sco! Scol

285
00:28:55.527 --> 00:28:57.768
stand up! Stand up!

286
00:28:57.862 --> 00:28:59.602
Come on. Stand up!

287
00:29:00.407 --> 00:29:02.113
Up! Up! Up!

288
00:29:03.410 --> 00:29:04.410
Come on!

289
00:29:04.995 --> 00:29:05.995
Stand up!

290
00:29:10.709 --> 00:29:12.245
The whole thing's coming down.

291
00:29:18.675 --> 00:29:20.381
You keep hold of me!

292
00:29:33.898 --> 00:29:35.638
We need to keep moving.

293
00:29:35.734 --> 00:29:37.065
Come on!

294
00:29:37.152 --> 00:29:39.108
I can't see. I can't see!

295
00:29:40.697 --> 00:29:42.858
Stop! Stop. stop. stop. stop! Stop!

296
00:29:43.658 --> 00:29:44.943
It's a mine shaft.

297
00:29:45.994 --> 00:29:47.325
We'll have to jump.

298
00:29:48.038 --> 00:29:49.244
All right. come on.

299
00:29:52.208 --> 00:29:54.574
You're going to have to jump.
Just jump.

300
00:29:54.669 --> 00:29:57.627
I can't. I can't see!
You need to trust me.

301
00:29:57.714 --> 00:29:58.714
Jump!

302
00:30:05.638 --> 00:30:08.175
Don't let go of me! Don't let go!

303
00:30:11.728 --> 00:30:13.434
Light! There's light.

304
00:30:25.533 --> 00:30:28.149
Stop. stop.

305
00:30:28.244 --> 00:30:29.575
Just let me stand.

306
00:30:33.166 --> 00:30:34.656
Dirty bastards!

307
00:30:40.507 --> 00:30:43.624
Careful. They may have left other traps.

308
00:30:52.477 --> 00:30:53.808
Jesus.

309
00:31:04.614 --> 00:31:07.572
Dust. So much dust in my eyes.

310
00:31:16.835 --> 00:31:18.371
Here.

311
00:31:18.461 --> 00:31:19.746
Have some of mine.

312
00:31:25.969 --> 00:31:27.880
I wish I'd shot that rat now.

313
00:31:29.097 --> 00:31:31.383
I wish you'd picked
some other bloody idiot.

314
00:31:32.016 --> 00:31:34.883
- What?
- Why in god's name did you choose me?

315
00:31:35.854 --> 00:31:39.187
- I didn't know what I was picking you for.
- No. you didn't.

316
00:31:39.274 --> 00:31:41.686
You never know.
That's your problem.

317
00:31:45.238 --> 00:31:46.444
All right. then go back.

318
00:31:47.907 --> 00:31:50.594
Nothing's stopping you. You can go
all the way bloody home if you want.

319
00:31:50.618 --> 00:31:51.618
Don't.

320
00:31:51.703 --> 00:31:52.818
Just don't.

321
00:31:54.831 --> 00:31:56.913
I didn't know what I was picking you for.

322
00:31:57.625 --> 00:32:01.117
I thought they were going to send us
back up the line or for food or something.

323
00:32:02.172 --> 00:32:05.460
I thought it was going to be
something easy. All right?

324
00:32:07.343 --> 00:32:09.004
I never thought it would be this.

325
00:32:15.977 --> 00:32:17.592
So. do you want to go back?

326
00:32:21.774 --> 00:32:23.389
Just fire the fucking flare.

327
00:32:39.000 --> 00:32:40.536
Up yours. lieutenant.

328
00:32:56.392 --> 00:32:57.677
Do you know where we are?

329
00:32:59.521 --> 00:33:02.934
Uh... ecoust is directly southeast.

330
00:33:04.651 --> 00:33:06.187
And if we keep that bearing...

331
00:33:07.445 --> 00:33:08.730
We should make it.

332
00:33:12.700 --> 00:33:13.700
Come on. then.

333
00:33:38.726 --> 00:33:39.761
Look at that.

334
00:33:40.645 --> 00:33:42.181
They destroyed their own guns.

335
00:33:43.523 --> 00:33:45.479
They destroyed their own trenches. too.

336
00:33:46.985 --> 00:33:48.646
What do you mean?

337
00:33:48.736 --> 00:33:51.193
Think they wanted us to go that way.

338
00:33:51.281 --> 00:33:52.896
They wanted to bury us.

339
00:34:00.290 --> 00:34:02.155
You bastard rats.

340
00:34:09.507 --> 00:34:13.295
Hey. did you hear that story
about wilko?

341
00:34:13.386 --> 00:34:15.718
- How he lost his ear?
- I'm not in the mood.

342
00:34:16.306 --> 00:34:18.888
Keep your eyes on the trees.
Top of the Ridge.

343
00:34:22.604 --> 00:34:24.185
Bet he told you it was shrapnel.

344
00:34:25.857 --> 00:34:27.597
What was it. then?

345
00:34:28.693 --> 00:34:32.060
Well. you know
his girl's a hairdresser. right?

346
00:34:32.905 --> 00:34:36.739
And he was moaning about the lack of
bathing facilities when he wrote to her.

347
00:34:37.535 --> 00:34:39.571
You remember
those rancid Jakes at arras?

348
00:34:39.662 --> 00:34:40.572
Yeah.

349
00:34:40.663 --> 00:34:43.700
Anyway. she sends him over this hair oll.

350
00:34:45.168 --> 00:34:48.251
Smells sweet. Like golden syrup.

351
00:34:50.298 --> 00:34:55.543
Wilko loves the smell. but he doesn't
want to cart it around in his pack.

352
00:34:56.638 --> 00:35:01.803
So he slathers it all over his barnet.
goes to sleep.

353
00:35:02.477 --> 00:35:05.093
and in the middle of the night
he wakes up.

354
00:35:05.188 --> 00:35:10.228
and a rat is sitting on his shoulder.
licking the oil off his head.

355
00:35:11.611 --> 00:35:14.148
Wilko panics. and he jumps up.

356
00:35:14.238 --> 00:35:17.696
And when he does. the rat bites
clean through his fucking ear

357
00:35:17.784 --> 00:35:20.116
- and runs off with it!
- No!

358
00:35:20.203 --> 00:35:23.912
He made a hell of a fuss.
yellin'. screamin'.

359
00:35:24.624 --> 00:35:28.037
The best of it was.
he'd put so much bloody oil on himself

360
00:35:28.127 --> 00:35:29.708
that he couldn't wash it off.

361
00:35:29.796 --> 00:35:31.627
He was like a magnet.

362
00:35:31.714 --> 00:35:34.376
Rats left us alone.
but they couldn't get enough of him.

363
00:35:34.467 --> 00:35:35.467
Poor bastard.

364
00:35:43.351 --> 00:35:44.636
Heading back home.

365
00:35:45.770 --> 00:35:47.180
I wonder what they saw.

366
00:35:49.565 --> 00:35:50.805
Watch the ridgelines.

367
00:35:55.988 --> 00:35:57.853
Well. that's your medal sorted. then.

368
00:35:59.200 --> 00:36:00.200
What do you mean?

369
00:36:01.077 --> 00:36:05.616
"Lance corporal Blake showed unusual valor
rescuing a comrade from certain death."

370
00:36:05.707 --> 00:36:06.947
Blah. blah. blah.

371
00:36:08.626 --> 00:36:09.626
You reckon?

372
00:36:10.712 --> 00:36:11.712
I do.

373
00:36:14.632 --> 00:36:17.419
Well. that'd be nice.
since you lost yours.

374
00:36:18.302 --> 00:36:19.633
I didn't lose mine.

375
00:36:21.139 --> 00:36:22.470
What happened to it. then?

376
00:36:22.932 --> 00:36:24.468
Why do you care?

377
00:36:24.559 --> 00:36:25.799
Why do you not?

378
00:36:27.895 --> 00:36:30.102
I swapped it with a French captain.

379
00:36:30.189 --> 00:36:32.350
- Swapped it?
- Mm-hmm.

380
00:36:32.442 --> 00:36:33.682
For what?

381
00:36:33.776 --> 00:36:34.856
Bottle of wine.

382
00:36:36.154 --> 00:36:37.860
What did you do that for?

383
00:36:37.947 --> 00:36:39.187
I was thirsty.

384
00:36:41.242 --> 00:36:42.402
What a waste.

385
00:36:44.829 --> 00:36:46.785
You should have
taken it home with you.

386
00:36:46.873 --> 00:36:49.330
You should have given it
to your family.

387
00:36:51.794 --> 00:36:53.204
Men have died for that.

388
00:36:55.089 --> 00:36:56.670
If I got a medal.
I'd take it home.

389
00:36:56.758 --> 00:37:00.250
- Why didn't you just take it home?
- Look. it's just a bit of bloody tin.

390
00:37:00.344 --> 00:37:01.925
It doesn't make you special.

391
00:37:02.013 --> 00:37:03.924
Doesn't make any difference
to anyone.

392
00:37:04.974 --> 00:37:05.974
Yes. it does.

393
00:37:07.226 --> 00:37:08.932
And it's not just a bit of tin.

394
00:37:09.020 --> 00:37:10.135
It's got a ribbon on it.

395
00:37:15.401 --> 00:37:16.891
I hated going home.

396
00:37:17.945 --> 00:37:19.151
I hated it.

397
00:37:21.199 --> 00:37:22.814
When I knew I couldn't stay...

398
00:37:23.993 --> 00:37:26.700
When I knew I had to leave
and they might never see m...

399
00:37:58.027 --> 00:37:59.027
Jesus.

400
00:38:02.406 --> 00:38:03.771
They chopped them all down.

401
00:38:08.079 --> 00:38:09.079
Cherries.

402
00:38:13.251 --> 00:38:14.251
Lamberts.

403
00:38:18.130 --> 00:38:19.336
They might be Dukes.

404
00:38:20.174 --> 00:38:22.130
Hard to tell when they aren't in fruit.

405
00:38:23.010 --> 00:38:24.216
What's the difference?

406
00:38:25.471 --> 00:38:27.382
Well. people think there's one type.

407
00:38:28.307 --> 00:38:29.513
But there's lots of them.

408
00:38:29.600 --> 00:38:34.219
Cuthberts. queen annes. montmorencys.
Sweet ones. sour ones.

409
00:38:34.313 --> 00:38:35.974
Why on earth
would you know this?

410
00:38:36.691 --> 00:38:38.272
Mum's got an orchard back home.

411
00:38:39.193 --> 00:38:40.353
Only a few trees.

412
00:38:41.654 --> 00:38:43.986
This time of year.
it looks like it's been snowing.

413
00:38:44.866 --> 00:38:46.072
Blossom everywhere.

414
00:38:47.702 --> 00:38:50.239
And then in may.
we have to pick them.

415
00:38:51.581 --> 00:38:52.581
Me and Joe.

416
00:38:54.458 --> 00:38:55.698
Takes the whole day.

417
00:38:57.086 --> 00:38:58.792
So. these ones all goners?

418
00:38:59.547 --> 00:39:02.710
Oh. no. They'll grow again
when the stones rot.

419
00:39:03.551 --> 00:39:05.667
You'll end up with more trees
than before.

420
00:39:11.309 --> 00:39:13.015
It looks abandoned.

421
00:39:13.102 --> 00:39:14.308
Let's hope so.

422
00:39:15.354 --> 00:39:16.685
We have to make sure.

423
00:39:49.805 --> 00:39:51.386
I'll take front. you take back.

424
00:40:34.308 --> 00:40:35.388
Anything?

425
00:40:36.268 --> 00:40:37.268
Nothing.

426
00:40:56.330 --> 00:40:57.740
Did you find any food?

427
00:40:57.832 --> 00:40:58.832
No.

428
00:41:00.459 --> 00:41:01.665
I don't like this place.

429
00:42:10.029 --> 00:42:15.569
Map says get over that Ridge
and it's a straight shot to ecoust.

430
00:42:17.161 --> 00:42:18.367
Good.

431
00:43:02.748 --> 00:43:04.079
Is that our friends again?

432
00:43:05.209 --> 00:43:06.415
Looks like it.

433
00:43:07.670 --> 00:43:08.670
Dogfight.

434
00:43:10.381 --> 00:43:12.246
Who's winning?

435
00:43:12.341 --> 00:43:13.376
Us. I think.

436
00:43:14.718 --> 00:43:15.718
Two on one.

437
00:43:19.723 --> 00:43:20.723
They got him.

438
00:44:19.783 --> 00:44:23.492
- We should put him out of his misery.
- No. Get him some water. He needs water.

439
00:44:24.622 --> 00:44:26.658
It's all right. It's all right.

440
00:44:27.583 --> 00:44:29.119
Steady. Stay still.

441
00:44:38.427 --> 00:44:40.008
Stop. Stop!

442
00:44:40.846 --> 00:44:42.711
No. No. no!

443
00:44:48.687 --> 00:44:51.645
You bastard!

444
00:44:51.732 --> 00:44:55.316
You bloody bastard.

445
00:44:57.112 --> 00:44:59.728
Oh. god. no.

446
00:44:59.823 --> 00:45:01.313
Oh. god. no!

447
00:45:02.993 --> 00:45:04.824
Jesus. Jesus. no!

448
00:45:06.121 --> 00:45:08.237
We have to stop the bleeding.

449
00:45:08.332 --> 00:45:09.868
Stop. Stop it! Stop it!

450
00:45:09.959 --> 00:45:11.824
It's all right.
It's going to be all right.

451
00:45:12.836 --> 00:45:13.996
We're going to stand up.

452
00:45:14.088 --> 00:45:16.044
- Okay. yes. Yes.
- Right?

453
00:45:20.594 --> 00:45:23.051
No. I can't. I can't. Ow!

454
00:45:24.640 --> 00:45:26.801
- We have to get to an aid post.
- I can't.

455
00:45:26.892 --> 00:45:29.850
- I'll carry you. It isn't very far.
- Just bring a doctor here.

456
00:45:29.937 --> 00:45:31.598
We can't. We have to go together.

457
00:45:33.315 --> 00:45:34.430
We're going to get up.

458
00:45:35.067 --> 00:45:36.273
We're going to get up.

459
00:45:42.491 --> 00:45:44.231
- Stop!
- Come on.

460
00:45:44.326 --> 00:45:45.326
Please stop!

461
00:45:46.120 --> 00:45:49.578
Put me down!
Put me down. you bastard. please!

462
00:45:49.665 --> 00:45:50.665
Put me down!

463
00:45:58.465 --> 00:46:00.251
Oh!

464
00:46:01.427 --> 00:46:03.167
You have to try to keep moving.

465
00:46:03.262 --> 00:46:04.752
Let's just sit.

466
00:46:04.847 --> 00:46:06.508
- Let me sit.
- No. we can't.

467
00:46:06.598 --> 00:46:08.304
We have to find the 2nd. remember?

468
00:46:08.392 --> 00:46:10.007
Your brother. We have to go now.

469
00:46:10.102 --> 00:46:12.013
You can start on without me.
I'll catch up.

470
00:46:12.104 --> 00:46:14.015
No. You can't stay here.

471
00:46:14.898 --> 00:46:17.139
We have to move. All right?

472
00:46:17.234 --> 00:46:19.520
We have to move. Now. come on.

473
00:46:19.611 --> 00:46:21.647
Come on!

474
00:46:21.739 --> 00:46:23.445
Come on. That's it.

475
00:46:23.532 --> 00:46:26.274
Come on. come on. Come on.

476
00:46:32.124 --> 00:46:34.831
Your brother.
We have to find your brother.

477
00:46:37.880 --> 00:46:38.960
You'll recognize him.

478
00:46:40.966 --> 00:46:42.672
He looks like me.

479
00:46:42.760 --> 00:46:45.376
And he's a bit older.

480
00:46:58.233 --> 00:46:59.233
What are they?

481
00:47:02.029 --> 00:47:03.485
Are we being shelled?

482
00:47:05.115 --> 00:47:07.356
They're embers. The barn is on fire.

483
00:47:12.748 --> 00:47:13.954
I've been hit.

484
00:47:16.043 --> 00:47:17.249
What was it?

485
00:47:18.712 --> 00:47:19.918
You were stabbed.

486
00:47:25.886 --> 00:47:27.467
Am I dying?

487
00:47:36.313 --> 00:47:37.313
Yes.

488
00:47:39.066 --> 00:47:40.306
Yes. I think you are.

489
00:47:58.001 --> 00:48:00.492
- This?
- Inside.

490
00:48:24.528 --> 00:48:26.814
Will you write to my mum for me?

491
00:48:28.323 --> 00:48:29.323
I will.

492
00:48:32.453 --> 00:48:33.909
Tell her I wasn't scared.

493
00:48:38.417 --> 00:48:39.417
Anything else?

494
00:48:42.463 --> 00:48:43.748
I love them.

495
00:48:46.175 --> 00:48:47.175
I wish that...

496
00:48:49.845 --> 00:48:51.085
I wish that...

497
00:48:57.394 --> 00:48:58.600
Talk to me.

498
00:49:01.315 --> 00:49:03.021
Tell me you know the way.

499
00:49:06.612 --> 00:49:07.772
I know the way.

500
00:49:09.573 --> 00:49:12.315
I'm going to head southeast
until I hit ecoust.

501
00:49:13.327 --> 00:49:14.817
I'll pass through the town

502
00:49:14.912 --> 00:49:17.745
and out to the east
all the way to croisilles wood.

503
00:49:18.790 --> 00:49:20.405
It'll be dark by then.

504
00:49:21.502 --> 00:49:22.582
That won't bother me.

505
00:49:23.879 --> 00:49:25.665
I'll find the 2nd.

506
00:49:25.756 --> 00:49:27.792
I'll give them the message.

507
00:49:27.883 --> 00:49:30.295
and then I'll find your brother.

508
00:49:30.385 --> 00:49:33.127
Just like you. a little older.

509
00:51:36.511 --> 00:51:37.796
You all right. mate?

510
00:51:39.014 --> 00:51:41.175
Hey. it's all right. It's okay.

511
00:51:42.184 --> 00:51:43.469
Come on. Help him.

512
00:51:52.819 --> 00:51:53.819
Jesus.

513
00:51:54.321 --> 00:51:55.401
What happened to him?

514
00:51:57.240 --> 00:52:00.152
Was it the plane?
We saw the smoke.

515
00:52:00.243 --> 00:52:01.243
Yeah.

516
00:52:18.261 --> 00:52:19.967
Go and fetch his things.

517
00:52:20.055 --> 00:52:21.055
Ae =o = tn

518
00:52:25.268 --> 00:52:26.268
a friend?

519
00:52:29.856 --> 00:52:31.062
What are you doing here?

520
00:52:32.067 --> 00:52:34.604
I have an urgent message
for the 2nd devons.

521
00:52:34.695 --> 00:52:36.777
Orders to stop
tomorrow morning's attack.

522
00:52:37.406 --> 00:52:39.192
And where are they stationed?

523
00:52:39.282 --> 00:52:40.522
Just beyond ecoust.

524
00:52:41.660 --> 00:52:42.660
Come with me.

525
00:52:49.459 --> 00:52:51.450
Come with me. corporal.
That's an order.

526
00:52:52.003 --> 00:52:54.665
We're passing through ecoust.
We can take you some of the way.

527
00:52:57.092 --> 00:52:58.092
Sir.

528
00:53:23.368 --> 00:53:24.949
Oh. come on. sergeant.

529
00:53:25.036 --> 00:53:26.697
Put more men at the base.

530
00:53:27.414 --> 00:53:29.530
At the trunk!
It'll be heavier there.

531
00:53:30.625 --> 00:53:31.831
Might be a tight squeeze.

532
00:53:31.918 --> 00:53:34.500
No. you're not
going to be able to just lift it.

533
00:53:34.588 --> 00:53:36.829
Pivot the front end to the left.

534
00:53:36.923 --> 00:53:39.380
Jesus. they don't
make things easy. do they?

535
00:53:39.468 --> 00:53:43.052
They could at least have retreated
with a bit of grace. Bastards.

536
00:53:43.138 --> 00:53:44.138
Sir.

537
00:53:44.723 --> 00:53:46.634
- You're not one of mine.
- No. sir.

538
00:53:46.725 --> 00:53:49.717
He has an urgent message
to deliver to the 2nd devons. sir.

539
00:53:49.811 --> 00:53:50.955
Can you get past it?

540
00:53:50.979 --> 00:53:52.469
- No. sir.
- Oh. for god's sake.

541
00:53:52.564 --> 00:53:53.804
Just move it!

542
00:53:54.900 --> 00:53:57.061
There's room in the casuals' truck. sir.

543
00:53:57.611 --> 00:53:59.818
- He has orders.
- Yes. yes. all right.

544
00:53:59.905 --> 00:54:02.442
Come on. now.
You can get through there sideways.

545
00:54:07.245 --> 00:54:08.576
How did you get here. sir?

546
00:54:09.247 --> 00:54:12.114
Crossed no-man's-land
just outside bapaume.

547
00:54:13.043 --> 00:54:14.249
Took us the whole night.

548
00:54:14.753 --> 00:54:16.835
Bumped into a couple of hun stragglers
on the way

549
00:54:16.922 --> 00:54:18.628
who made a nuisance of themselves.

550
00:54:19.216 --> 00:54:21.753
- You going up to the new line?
- Attempting to.

551
00:54:22.594 --> 00:54:25.961
The newfoundlands have pushed forwards
and requested reinforcements.

552
00:54:28.058 --> 00:54:29.594
I'm sorry about your friend.

553
00:54:31.228 --> 00:54:34.015
May I tell you something
that you probably already know?

554
00:54:36.024 --> 00:54:37.730
It doesn't do to dwell on it.

555
00:54:38.985 --> 00:54:40.100
No. sir.

556
00:54:41.154 --> 00:54:44.112
Hop on.

557
00:54:44.199 --> 00:54:45.439
Make some space there.

558
00:54:47.869 --> 00:54:48.984
Come on. In you get!

559
00:55:05.846 --> 00:55:08.258
All right. Here we go again. boys.

560
00:55:11.226 --> 00:55:14.434
Welcome aboard the night bus
to fuck knows where.

561
00:55:18.233 --> 00:55:19.439
Is that a dead dog?

562
00:55:21.444 --> 00:55:23.355
- You got a fag?
- Yeah. There you go.

563
00:55:40.005 --> 00:55:43.247
- Butler. oi. Carry on with that story.
- Oh. yeah.

564
00:55:43.341 --> 00:55:46.174
Right. so. when we get off the train.

565
00:55:46.803 --> 00:55:49.670
beaufoy comes up to us
and he's having a right go.

566
00:55:50.932 --> 00:55:54.299
"Lance corporal. whatever one does.
one never lets standards slip."

567
00:55:54.394 --> 00:55:56.350
Then Scott comes out the latrine.

568
00:55:56.438 --> 00:55:58.895
He wipes his hand
on the back of beaufoy's jacket.

569
00:55:58.982 --> 00:56:01.348
Shit all down his back.

570
00:56:01.443 --> 00:56:05.106
- Was that meant to be captain beaufoy?
- Piss off. you. You can't do any better.

571
00:56:05.947 --> 00:56:08.484
"Men. your rifle stocks
are an embarrassment

572
00:56:08.575 --> 00:56:10.440
to the entire expeditionary force!"

573
00:56:10.535 --> 00:56:11.741
- Nah.
- No.

574
00:56:11.828 --> 00:56:13.443
You're both bloody awful.

575
00:56:13.538 --> 00:56:15.950
You don't know.
You barely even speak the bloody language.

576
00:56:16.041 --> 00:56:17.841
He's got a better grasp of it
than you. Cooke.

577
00:56:17.918 --> 00:56:19.283
Go on. jondalar. Give it a go.

578
00:56:19.377 --> 00:56:21.959
- Let's hear it. jonny.
- Let's hear it. Go on.

579
00:56:22.422 --> 00:56:26.085
"Rossi!
Never in my 200 years as a soldier

580
00:56:26.176 --> 00:56:28.758
have I seen such a sorry excuse
for a latrine pit!"

581
00:56:28.845 --> 00:56:31.882
Shite. That is total shit.

582
00:56:32.807 --> 00:56:36.550
Could've taken my teeth out with that.
You could do with a new set.

583
00:56:41.775 --> 00:56:43.436
You got somewhere
you need to be?

584
00:56:46.196 --> 00:56:48.437
- No.
- Arsehole needs driving lessons.

585
00:57:04.214 --> 00:57:06.045
He should reverse. Yeah.

586
00:57:07.634 --> 00:57:08.794
Try it in reverse.

587
00:57:09.719 --> 00:57:11.300
Reverse!

588
00:57:18.561 --> 00:57:21.052
No. Stop. Stop!

589
00:57:21.147 --> 00:57:22.603
Everyone needs to get out.

590
00:57:23.733 --> 00:57:24.733
All out!

591
00:57:26.569 --> 00:57:28.434
- Come on!
- All right. all right.

592
00:57:28.530 --> 00:57:29.861
Keep your bloody hair on.

593
00:57:30.907 --> 00:57:31.907
Right.

594
00:57:32.534 --> 00:57:35.196
One. two. three!

595
00:57:42.335 --> 00:57:44.271
We need to get some wood.
put it under the wheels.

596
00:57:44.295 --> 00:57:46.752
No. we haven't got the time.
We all need to push.

597
00:57:46.840 --> 00:57:48.455
Come on. Come on!

598
00:57:49.926 --> 00:57:51.587
Come on!

599
00:57:55.473 --> 00:57:58.465
Please! I have to go now. Please.

600
00:58:00.854 --> 00:58:03.095
All right. come on. lads.
Come on.

601
00:58:03.189 --> 00:58:04.349
Come on. boys.

602
00:58:04.441 --> 00:58:06.853
One. two. three.

603
00:58:18.580 --> 00:58:20.616
Come on. boys!
One last push. yeah?

604
00:58:20.707 --> 00:58:22.789
One. two. three!

605
00:58:35.930 --> 00:58:39.297
Back in. Get back in. Go.

606
00:58:40.894 --> 00:58:42.009
Are you all right?

607
00:58:43.271 --> 00:58:46.513
Here. driver. how about you try to keep it
on the bloody road for a change?

608
00:58:46.608 --> 00:58:47.939
Oh. piss off!

609
00:59:07.170 --> 00:59:08.535
So. where are you going?

610
00:59:10.298 --> 00:59:12.789
I have to get to the 2nd devons.
just past ecoust.

611
00:59:14.135 --> 00:59:15.135
Why?

612
00:59:16.137 --> 00:59:17.923
They're attacking at dawn.

613
00:59:18.014 --> 00:59:19.595
I have orders to stop them.

614
00:59:19.682 --> 00:59:20.717
How come?

615
00:59:22.268 --> 00:59:24.975
- They're walking into a trap.
- How many?

616
00:59:26.106 --> 00:59:28.188
Sixteen hundred.

617
00:59:29.609 --> 00:59:30.609
Jesus.

618
00:59:33.071 --> 00:59:34.777
Why did they send you
on your own?

619
00:59:36.241 --> 00:59:37.241
They didn't.

620
00:59:37.951 --> 00:59:39.361
There were two of us.

621
00:59:40.453 --> 00:59:41.738
So. now it's down to you.

622
00:59:42.789 --> 00:59:43.789
Yes.

623
00:59:45.166 --> 00:59:46.281
You'll never make it.

624
00:59:50.922 --> 00:59:52.082
Yes. I will.

625
00:59:58.930 --> 00:59:59.930
Thank you.

626
01:00:02.809 --> 01:00:03.809
Look at it.

627
01:00:04.769 --> 01:00:05.884
Fucking look at it.

628
01:00:07.480 --> 01:00:09.061
Three years fightin' over this.

629
01:00:10.316 --> 01:00:12.432
We should've just
let the bastards keep it.

630
01:00:13.278 --> 01:00:16.770
- I mean. who machine-guns cows?
- Huns with extra bullets.

631
01:00:17.574 --> 01:00:18.780
Bastards.

632
01:00:19.993 --> 01:00:21.153
Clever.

633
01:00:21.244 --> 01:00:23.280
They know if they don't shoot the cow...

634
01:00:24.330 --> 01:00:25.945
You will eat it.

635
01:00:26.040 --> 01:00:27.280
Still bastards.

636
01:00:27.375 --> 01:00:29.457
Yeah. it's not even
our bloody country.

637
01:00:30.044 --> 01:00:32.501
- How long gone do you reckon they are?
- Why?

638
01:00:33.256 --> 01:00:36.123
Worried we'll catch up with them?
Yeah.

639
01:00:36.217 --> 01:00:38.424
Right. Be a bloody miracle at this rate.

640
01:00:38.511 --> 01:00:40.718
Yeah. they're probably
right round the next corner.

641
01:00:40.805 --> 01:00:42.386
Piss off. No. they're not.

642
01:00:43.641 --> 01:00:46.508
Why don't they just
bloody well give up? Eh?

643
01:00:47.812 --> 01:00:51.100
- Don't they wanna go home?
- They hate their wives and mothers.

644
01:00:51.191 --> 01:00:54.433
And Germany must be a shithole.

645
01:00:55.278 --> 01:00:56.814
They're retreatin'.

646
01:00:56.905 --> 01:00:58.486
They're miles back.

647
01:00:58.573 --> 01:01:00.154
Got 'em on the ropes. at least.

648
01:01:01.201 --> 01:01:03.943
No. We don't.

649
01:01:06.497 --> 01:01:08.237
Oh. bollocks. What's up now?

650
01:01:08.333 --> 01:01:11.370
- Not another bloody tree.
- The bridge is down.

651
01:01:11.461 --> 01:01:13.793
Oh. That's a shame.

652
01:01:13.880 --> 01:01:15.916
Looks like I'll be getting out here.

653
01:01:16.007 --> 01:01:17.007
Good luck.

654
01:01:17.800 --> 01:01:19.836
Keep some of that luck
for yourself. pal.

655
01:01:19.928 --> 01:01:21.614
- Think you'll be needing it.
- Good luck. mate.

656
01:01:21.638 --> 01:01:24.095
Good luck. guv.
Don't balls it up.

657
01:01:25.016 --> 01:01:26.426
I hope you get there.

658
01:01:27.894 --> 01:01:28.894
Thank you.

659
01:01:32.732 --> 01:01:35.940
The next bridge is six miles.
We'll have to divert.

660
01:01:36.027 --> 01:01:38.484
I can't. sir. I don't have the time.

661
01:01:39.405 --> 01:01:40.565
Of course.

662
01:01:42.533 --> 01:01:43.533
Best of luck.

663
01:01:44.619 --> 01:01:45.619
Thank you. sir.

664
01:01:49.374 --> 01:01:50.374
Corporal?

665
01:01:51.542 --> 01:01:53.828
If you do manage
to get to colonel MacKenzie...

666
01:01:55.338 --> 01:01:56.874
Make sure there are withesses.

667
01:01:58.299 --> 01:02:00.290
- They are direct orders. sir.
- I know.

668
01:02:02.053 --> 01:02:04.044
But some men just want the fight.

669
01:02:06.808 --> 01:02:07.923
Thank you. sir.

670
01:02:12.563 --> 01:02:15.430
Driver! Move off!

671
01:12:53.746 --> 01:12:55.862
Anglais.

672
01:12:55.956 --> 01:12:57.742
Not German.

673
01:12:57.833 --> 01:12:58.833
Friend.

674
01:12:59.668 --> 01:13:00.874
I'm a friend.

675
01:13:04.256 --> 01:13:06.417
This place. this town...

676
01:13:07.259 --> 01:13:08.259
Ecoust?

677
01:13:18.354 --> 01:13:19.354
Others?

678
01:13:20.022 --> 01:13:21.762
No. Just me.

679
01:13:24.526 --> 01:13:25.732
Only me.

680
01:13:28.989 --> 01:13:30.479
I need to be somewhere.

681
01:13:31.909 --> 01:13:34.901
I need to find a wood to the southeast.

682
01:13:36.956 --> 01:13:38.787
Uh. trees.

683
01:13:42.962 --> 01:13:44.168
Croiset?

684
01:13:44.254 --> 01:13:45.414
Croisilles?

685
01:13:45.506 --> 01:13:46.506
Yes.

686
01:13:50.636 --> 01:13:51.967
River.

687
01:13:52.054 --> 01:13:55.091
River. It go there.

688
01:13:56.016 --> 01:13:58.007
Trees. Croisilles.

689
01:14:35.431 --> 01:14:36.796
Shh.

690
01:14:37.850 --> 01:14:38.885
Shh.

691
01:15:30.986 --> 01:15:31.986
Thank you.

692
01:15:59.765 --> 01:16:01.096
A girl?

693
