We've got them on the run!

788
01:34:30.833 --> 01:34:32.573
You don't.
Please don't send your men over.

789
01:34:32.668 --> 01:34:33.668
Get out of the way!

790
01:34:33.711 --> 01:34:36.748
These are direct orders from army command!
Where is colonel MacKenzie?

791
01:34:36.839 --> 01:34:39.546
Jesus Christ. man!
Go and see the captain!

792
01:34:39.634 --> 01:34:41.915
Now. I want us up there quickly.
you understand?

793
01:34:41.969 --> 01:34:44.585
- Do you understand?
- Yes. sirl

794
01:34:45.723 --> 01:34:48.430
ncos collect flares and signal flags.
Keep to your stations.

795
01:34:48.517 --> 01:34:49.927
Oi. Oil

796
01:34:58.444 --> 01:35:00.981
Nine and ten section at the ready!

797
01:35:01.739 --> 01:35:04.981
We will advance
on the first whistle blast!

798
01:35:07.370 --> 01:35:09.577
The man next to you falls. keep moving.

799
01:35:09.664 --> 01:35:11.825
Your orders are to break the lines.

800
01:35:11.916 --> 01:35:14.248
- Where is the captain?
- He's over there.

801
01:35:16.629 --> 01:35:18.620
Sir! Sir!

802
01:35:20.132 --> 01:35:22.373
Captain. I have a message.

803
01:35:22.468 --> 01:35:23.878
This attack is called off.

804
01:35:23.970 --> 01:35:26.302
You have to stop.
You have to stop.

805
01:35:30.226 --> 01:35:31.682
Where is colonel MacKenzie?

806
01:35:32.311 --> 01:35:34.472
Where is MacKenzie?

807
01:36:04.385 --> 01:36:06.501
Back! Hold fast!

808
01:36:08.973 --> 01:36:12.136
Sir. I have orders to stop this attack!

809
01:36:12.226 --> 01:36:13.226
What?

810
01:36:13.311 --> 01:36:15.643
Where is colonel MacKenzie?

811
01:36:15.730 --> 01:36:17.436
He's further up the line.

812
01:36:17.523 --> 01:36:18.433
How far?

813
01:36:18.524 --> 01:36:21.061
Three hundred yards.
He's in a cut-and-cover.

814
01:36:21.152 --> 01:36:23.859
You'll have to wait
until the first wave goes over.

815
01:36:23.946 --> 01:36:25.902
No. No. I can't.

816
01:36:33.664 --> 01:36:37.077
Seven platoon. 30 seconds!

817
01:36:48.804 --> 01:36:52.092
You can't possibly make it that way. man!
Are you bloody insane?

818
01:36:56.729 --> 01:36:58.890
What the hell are you doing.
Lance corporal?

819
01:36:59.357 --> 01:37:01.097
No! No. no. no. no!

820
01:38:05.923 --> 01:38:07.413
Get ready!

821
01:38:07.508 --> 01:38:09.669
- Colonel MacKenzie!
- He's in there.

822
01:38:11.429 --> 01:38:12.509
Two minutes!

823
01:38:13.013 --> 01:38:14.013
Let me through!

824
01:38:14.098 --> 01:38:15.759
Hey! Hey!

825
01:38:15.850 --> 01:38:18.683
Let me through! I have to get through!

826
01:38:18.769 --> 01:38:20.038
I have to see colonel MacKenzie!

827
01:38:20.062 --> 01:38:21.790
- What are you doing?
- I have to stop this attack!

828
01:38:21.814 --> 01:38:22.974
Colonel. we've seen flares.

829
01:38:23.065 --> 01:38:25.185
Men on the left flank
have made it to the German line.

830
01:38:25.276 --> 01:38:27.562
- Colonel! Colonel!
- Hold him! Hold him!

831
01:38:27.653 --> 01:38:29.894
Listen to me.
Listen to me. I have a letter.

832
01:38:29.989 --> 01:38:31.570
I need to see colonel MacKenzie.

833
01:38:31.657 --> 01:38:33.343
There's no bloody way
you're gettin' in there!

834
01:38:33.367 --> 01:38:34.982
Sergeant. send the next wave!

835
01:38:35.077 --> 01:38:36.192
No!

836
01:38:36.287 --> 01:38:38.323
Second wave. prepare yourselves!

837
01:38:38.414 --> 01:38:40.392
- Colonel MacKenzie!
- Concentrate everything there.

838
01:38:40.416 --> 01:38:42.657
This attack is not to go ahead!

839
01:38:42.751 --> 01:38:45.458
You have been ordered to stop!
You have to stop!

840
01:38:45.546 --> 01:38:46.877
Who the hell are you?

841
01:38:47.423 --> 01:38:49.755
Lance corporal Schofield. sir. 8th.

842
01:38:49.842 --> 01:38:52.584
I have orders from general erinmore
to call off this attack.

843
01:38:52.678 --> 01:38:54.088
You're too late. Lance corporal.

844
01:38:54.180 --> 01:38:57.672
Sir. these orders are from army command.
You have to read them.

845
01:38:57.766 --> 01:39:00.829
- Shall we hold back the second wave. sir?
- No. major. Hesitate now and we lose.

846
01:39:00.853 --> 01:39:03.060
Victory's only 500 yards away.
=sirl

847
01:39:03.147 --> 01:39:04.307
please. read the letter.

848
01:39:04.398 --> 01:39:07.356
I have heard it all before.

849
01:39:07.443 --> 01:39:09.525
I'm not gonna wait until dusk or for fog.

850
01:39:09.612 --> 01:39:12.412
I'm not calling back my men only
to send them out there again tomorrow.

851
01:39:12.448 --> 01:39:14.009
not when we've got the bastards
on the run.

852
01:39:14.033 --> 01:39:16.649
- This is their last stand.
- The Germans planned this. sir.

853
01:39:18.078 --> 01:39:21.411
They've been planning it for months.
They want you to attack.

854
01:39:22.625 --> 01:39:23.865
Read the letter.

855
01:39:44.605 --> 01:39:46.220
- Major?
- Yes. sir?

856
01:39:48.817 --> 01:39:50.023
Stand them down.

857
01:39:50.819 --> 01:39:52.275
- Yes. sir.
- Call up the orderlies.

858
01:39:52.363 --> 01:39:53.694
Tend the wounded.

859
01:39:53.781 --> 01:39:55.362
Hold the line
in case they counter.

860
01:39:55.449 --> 01:39:56.939
Yes. sir!

861
01:39:57.034 --> 01:39:59.446
Stand down! Stand down!

862
01:40:02.581 --> 01:40:05.789
Stand down!

863
01:40:05.876 --> 01:40:09.118
- Cease fire! Cease fire!
- Stand down!

864
01:40:13.092 --> 01:40:15.458
I hoped today
might be a good day.

865
01:40:17.805 --> 01:40:20.137
Hope is a dangerous thing.

866
01:40:22.268 --> 01:40:25.601
That's it for now. and then next week
command will send a different message.

867
01:40:26.605 --> 01:40:27.845
"Attack at dawn."

868
01:40:31.777 --> 01:40:33.768
There is only one way this war ends.

869
01:40:36.323 --> 01:40:38.109
Last man standing.

870
01:40:43.831 --> 01:40:45.446
Have someone see to your wounds.

871
01:40:48.544 --> 01:40:50.626
Now. fuck off. Lance corporal.

872
01:40:56.510 --> 01:40:59.798
Bearers! Stretcher bearers!

873
01:41:00.848 --> 01:41:03.965
Bearers! Stretcher bearers!

874
01:41:04.643 --> 01:41:05.849
Well done. lad.

875
01:41:07.062 --> 01:41:08.177
Thank you. sir.

876
01:41:10.649 --> 01:41:12.560
Do you know where
lieutenant Blake is. sir?

877
01:41:13.110 --> 01:41:14.646
Blake?

878
01:41:14.737 --> 01:41:16.568
There were two of us.

879
01:41:16.655 --> 01:41:18.896
I was sent here with his brother.

880
01:41:18.991 --> 01:41:20.106
Ah.

881
01:41:21.201 --> 01:41:24.739
Well. knowing lieutenant Blake.
he would have gone over with his men.

882
01:41:24.830 --> 01:41:26.366
He was in the first wave.

883
01:41:28.000 --> 01:41:29.865
How could I find him. sir?

884
01:41:29.960 --> 01:41:33.202
You can try the casualty clearing station
behind the line.

885
01:41:34.840 --> 01:41:36.046
Otherwise...

886
01:41:39.511 --> 01:41:40.671
Thank you. sir.

887
01:41:41.555 --> 01:41:42.886
Major hepburn. sir!

888
01:42:34.316 --> 01:42:37.308
Just keep movin'.
Keep movin'. keep movin'.

889
01:43:02.469 --> 01:43:05.802
Sergeant. I have to find lieutenant Blake.
Do you know where he is?

890
01:43:05.889 --> 01:43:06.889
No.

891
01:43:27.077 --> 01:43:28.192
Clear the way.

892
01:43:28.787 --> 01:43:32.245
- Sir. is lieutenant Blake here?
- No idea.

893
01:43:33.709 --> 01:43:34.869
Move along. corporal.

894
01:43:36.462 --> 01:43:38.544
If you can walk. move to the triage area.

895
01:43:40.716 --> 01:43:43.674
Help me!

896
01:43:46.430 --> 01:43:47.545
Lieutenant Blake!

897
01:43:51.059 --> 01:43:54.392
Sir. he's out.

898
01:43:57.024 --> 01:43:58.560
Out of the bloody way!

899
01:43:59.943 --> 01:44:01.183
Blake?

900
01:44:03.822 --> 01:44:05.904
Has anyone seen lieutenant Blake?

901
01:44:07.785 --> 01:44:10.743
He's hemorrhaging.
Go quickly. He needs a surgeon.

902
01:44:17.544 --> 01:44:19.580
Amputation. Straight to surgery.

903
01:44:24.426 --> 01:44:25.586
My leg!

904
01:44:28.722 --> 01:44:30.428
I need some help here! Quickly!

905
01:44:35.270 --> 01:44:37.352
I need something now!

906
01:44:41.193 --> 01:44:42.603
Coming through!

907
01:44:56.500 --> 01:44:58.331
All right. come on. boys.

908
01:44:58.418 --> 01:45:01.330
He's taken one in the leg.
He's lost a lot of blood.

909
01:45:01.421 --> 01:45:02.331
Sir.

910
01:45:02.422 --> 01:45:04.504
Lieutenant Blake? Yes?

911
01:45:06.385 --> 01:45:07.966
Do you need medical assistance?

912
01:45:09.555 --> 01:45:12.547
No. sir. I'm from the 8th.

913
01:45:12.641 --> 01:45:14.302
What the hell are you doing here?

914
01:45:15.269 --> 01:45:18.136
- I was sent here to deliver a message.
- The 8th?

915
01:45:18.230 --> 01:45:19.595
You must know my brother.

916
01:45:20.941 --> 01:45:23.933
- I was sent here with him.
- Tom's here? Where is he?

917
01:45:30.617 --> 01:45:31.982
It was very quick.

918
01:45:34.621 --> 01:45:35.827
I'm sorry.

919
01:45:59.980 --> 01:46:01.140
What's your name?

920
01:46:02.316 --> 01:46:03.431
Schofield. sir.

921
01:46:06.904 --> 01:46:08.144
Sorry. what?

922
01:46:08.947 --> 01:46:10.733
It's Schofield. sir.

923
01:46:10.824 --> 01:46:12.030
William Schofield.

924
01:46:13.410 --> 01:46:14.490
Will.

925
01:46:16.914 --> 01:46:20.031
Well. you need some food.
Get yourself to the mess tent.

926
01:46:35.057 --> 01:46:36.057
If I may...

927
01:46:37.142 --> 01:46:38.803
I'd like to write to your mother.

928
01:46:39.895 --> 01:46:41.886
Tell her that Tom wasn't alone.

929
01:46:45.442 --> 01:46:46.442
Of course.

930
01:46:49.279 --> 01:46:50.279
He was...

931
01:46:52.240 --> 01:46:53.571
He was a good man.

932
01:46:55.786 --> 01:46:57.367
Always telling funny stories.

933
01:47:00.540 --> 01:47:01.871
He saved my life.

934
01:47:06.046 --> 01:47:08.037
I am glad you were with him.

935
01:47:14.304 --> 01:47:15.419
Thank you. will.

935
01:47:16.305 --> 01:48:16.445
